WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.668
The ceremony will begin

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.970
with an address by the secretary general.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:05.405
 

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.273
 

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.542
 

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:12.679
President

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.180
Niinisto

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.683
Sauli. Ministers.

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.686
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:00:19.686 --> 00:00:21.755
this is an historic day.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:25.058
We welcome Finland as the newest

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:28.495
member of our alliance.

00:00:28.495 --> 00:00:31.097
We will raise the Finnish flag

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:33.033
for the first time

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:36.269
here at the NATO headquarters.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:39.372
31 flags flying together

00:00:39.406 --> 00:00:41.408
as a symbol of our unity

00:00:41.641 --> 00:00:44.477
and our solidarity.

00:00:44.811 --> 00:00:46.346
On this day,

00:00:46.346 --> 00:00:49.282
on the 4th of April, 1949

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.218
the Washington Treaty was signed

00:00:53.253 --> 00:00:55.221
to create a shield

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:56.756
against aggression

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:59.359
and the fear of aggression.

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.728
For almost 75 years,

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:05.398
this great alliance has shielded

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.502
our nations and it continues to do so.

00:01:09.536 --> 00:01:10.470
Today

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:15.608
but war has returned to Europe,

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.813
and Finland has decided to join NATO

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:22.082
and be part of the world's

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.850
most successful alliance.

00:01:26.086 --> 00:01:27.454
This has been the

00:01:27.454 --> 00:01:29.355
fastest accession

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.791
process in NATO's modern history.

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:35.995
Finland and Sweden applied for membership

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.331
last May in June

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:40.600
after a summit in Madrid.

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.735
Every ally invited them to join.

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:45.772
And today, less than a year later,

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.841
we welcome Finland

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:50.443
as a full member of our alliance.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:54.614
I look forward to also welcoming

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.883
Sweden into the alliance

00:01:56.883 --> 00:01:59.853
as soon as possible.

00:01:59.853 --> 00:02:01.955
Finland is safer

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:06.426
and is stronger with Finland as an ally.

00:02:07.961 --> 00:02:10.563
Your forces are substantial

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.899
and highly capable.

00:02:12.899 --> 00:02:15.502
Your resilience is second to none

00:02:16.269 --> 00:02:19.372
and for many years, troops in Finland

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:19.906
and NATO's

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:21.241
countries have worked

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:23.343
side by side as partners.

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:27.347
From today, we stand together as allies.

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:31.351
This sends a clear message

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.553
that every nation has the right

00:02:33.553 --> 00:02:35.788
to choose its own path.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.857
That need to store remains open,

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.160
and no one can close it

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.728
with force or coercion.

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.300
Naito is a community

00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.171
united by our values freedom, democracy,

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.739
and the rule of law.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:54.541
We stand together.

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.910
We protect and defend each other,

00:02:57.544 --> 00:03:00.513
all for one and one for all.

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:04.317
President.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:07.153
Minister Howley,

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.522
I'm glad to be here together with you

00:03:10.023 --> 00:03:12.692
on this great day.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.595
Thank you for your outstanding leadership

00:03:16.296 --> 00:03:18.264
and your tireless work

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:21.935
to make this day possible.

00:03:21.935 --> 00:03:23.269
I'm glad and I'm

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:25.939
proud to be the Secretary General

00:03:26.272 --> 00:03:27.840
that welcomes Finland

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.476
fully into the Naito family.

00:03:31.044 --> 00:03:34.914
Welcome to the Alliance

00:03:51.331 --> 00:03:52.732
The President of Finland

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.968
will now deliver his address mat,

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:56.703
not the president that I felt alone

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:57.570
but can't open up.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.204
I heard

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.108
Secretary General Stoltenberg.

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.344
Dear Defense

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:05.912
Ministers,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.514
Excellencies, ladies and gentlemen,

00:04:09.716 --> 00:04:12.752
Phil Lord has today become the 31st

00:04:12.952 --> 00:04:16.322
member of NATO's

00:04:16.389 --> 00:04:18.458
the era of military.

00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:22.395
Non-Alignment in our history has come

00:04:22.395 --> 00:04:23.930
to an end.

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.865
A new era begins

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:28.501
Each country

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:31.070
maximizes its own security.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:33.906
So does Finland.

00:04:33.906 --> 00:04:34.941
Later, membership

00:04:34.941 --> 00:04:37.777
strengthens our international position

00:04:38.077 --> 00:04:41.147
and room for maneuver.

00:04:41.948 --> 00:04:44.851
As a partner, we have already long

00:04:45.084 --> 00:04:45.952
actively

00:04:45.952 --> 00:04:49.188
participated in NATO's activities.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:53.226
As an ally, Finland will contribute

00:04:53.459 --> 00:04:54.193
to NATO's

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:57.230
collective deterrence and defense

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.401
Membership of the alliance

00:05:01.401 --> 00:05:04.070
provides security for Finland.

00:05:04.871 --> 00:05:05.505
Finland,

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:08.474
on the other hand, to provide security

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.911
for the alliance.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:14.981
Finland, committed to the security

00:05:14.981 --> 00:05:17.583
of all NATO's member states,

00:05:17.583 --> 00:05:20.119
will be a reliable ally

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.556
that strengthens regional

00:05:23.723 --> 00:05:25.525
stability

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.494
Finland's membership

00:05:28.494 --> 00:05:31.064
is not targeted against anyone,

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.901
nor does it change the foundations

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:36.703
or objectives

00:05:36.703 --> 00:05:40.073
of Finland's foreign and security policy.

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:43.376
Finland's a stable and predictable

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:46.112
Nordic country that seeks peaceful

00:05:46.379 --> 00:05:49.048
resolution of disputes.

00:05:50.283 --> 00:05:52.051
The principles and values

00:05:52.051 --> 00:05:54.187
that are important to Finland

00:05:54.454 --> 00:05:55.555
will continue

00:05:55.555 --> 00:05:57.623
to guide our foreign policy

00:05:57.623 --> 00:05:59.292
also in the future.

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:02.862
NATO's

00:06:02.862 --> 00:06:03.596
membership, but

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:06.132
does not change everything.

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:09.802
But being an ally requires Finland

00:06:09.802 --> 00:06:12.105
to adopt new ways of thinking

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:16.709
and some changes in legislation as well.

00:06:17.910 --> 00:06:21.381
A lot has already been done For years

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:25.318
we have developed our NATO compatibility.

00:06:26.319 --> 00:06:28.755
There's still considerable work ahead

00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:30.790
to integrate Finland's

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:35.194
defense as part of NATO's common defense.

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:38.765
The Finnish defense forces are facing

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:42.902
new demands and challenges to which

00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:45.638
we must respond

00:06:48.074 --> 00:06:49.375
At the same time,

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:50.042
it is clear

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:50.777
that Finland's

00:06:50.777 --> 00:06:53.946
most significant contribution to NATO's

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.648
collective deterrence

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.483
and defense is built

00:06:57.483 --> 00:06:58.851
on the security

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:02.155
and defense of our own territory.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.690
In this respect,

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.793
the Finland finish concept

00:07:07.560 --> 00:07:10.163
of comprehensive security

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:13.933
retains its value,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:17.303
but we no longer do this work alone.

00:07:18.938 --> 00:07:20.773
Last year, Finland applied

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:23.209
to join NATO together with Sweden.

00:07:23.976 --> 00:07:26.679
As I have stressed, Finland to

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:29.282
membership is not complete without

00:07:29.348 --> 00:07:30.683
that of Sweden.

00:07:31.717 --> 00:07:33.719
Our persistent efforts

00:07:33.719 --> 00:07:34.053
for a

00:07:34.053 --> 00:07:37.190
rapid Swedish membership will continue.

00:07:38.257 --> 00:07:40.593
I look forward to seeing Sweden

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:45.031
to join us as the 32nd

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:48.868
member at the Vilnius Summit in July.

00:07:50.536 --> 00:07:53.239
To add up, I want to thank you, Mr.

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:55.141
Secretary-General.

00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:57.176
Dear Jens and your people.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:08:00.413
Your help has been

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:02.648
very important.

00:08:02.648 --> 00:08:04.350
You have been

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:06.419
backing us in

00:08:06.419 --> 00:08:09.055
every moment of this procedure.

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:11.657
We really gave a lot of value to that

00:08:11.924 --> 00:08:13.826
and to our partners.

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:14.827
Thank you.

